    "['map mpls l2vpn [vpn_name] ce [ce_id] ce-offset [offset_value]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'pseudowire-class VPN1-PW', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Huawei configuration:\\n\\n##\\npseudowire-class VPN1-PW\\n encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n \\nThe Huawei command `map mpls l2vpn vpn1 ce 2 ce-offset 1` is part of their MPLS L2VPN configuration that creates a mapping between the VPN instance and the customer edge (CE) interface. In Cisco, this would typically be configured as a pseudowire class that specifies MPLS encapsulation for the L2VPN connection.\\n\\nNote that Cisco's implementation is somewhat different architecturally - the complete L2VPN configuration would require additional commands (like xconnect configuration on the interface) to fully replicate the Huawei functionality. The pseudowire-class is the closest direct equivalent to this particular mapping command.\", 'trans_template': 'pseudowire-class VPN1-PW'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'encapsulation mpls', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'pseudowire-class [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Huawei configuration:\\n\\n##\\npseudowire-class VPN1-PW\\n encapsulation mpls\\n##\\n \\nThe Huawei command `map mpls l2vpn vpn1 ce 2 ce-offset 1` is part of their MPLS L2VPN configuration that creates a mapping between the VPN instance and the customer edge (CE) interface. In Cisco, this would typically be configured as a pseudowire class that specifies MPLS encapsulation for the L2VPN connection.\\n\\nNote that Cisco's implementation is somewhat different architecturally - the complete L2VPN configuration would require additional commands (like xconnect configuration on the interface) to fully replicate the Huawei functionality. The pseudowire-class is the closest direct equivalent to this p